cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use limen, please cite it as below."
title: "limen: the same-configuration noise floor of an evaluation"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Kurath"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KurathSec/limen"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - flakiness
  - noise floor
  - benchmark
abstract: >-
  An analyzer over repeated identical evaluation runs: per-item verdict
  flakiness (TARa@N), model-pair sign-stability rulings, the minimum
  detectable difference at the observed number of repeats, and a CI gate that
  fails a benchmark report claiming a gain smaller than that report's own
  measured draw noise. It makes no statement about which model is better.
